WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:09.220
Will the upcoming North-South summit at
Panmunjom usher in a new era of Korean

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:13.610
peace and denuclearization? Seoul's
Sunshine – or engagement-oriented –

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:17.210
government certainly seems to think so,
and there are many in America and

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:20.900
elsewhere who seem to agree – including
even president Donald Trump (at least

00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:25.789
from time to time). But let's not break
out the champagne just yet. The first two

00:00:25.789 --> 00:00:30.529
North-South summits in 2000 and 2007
were flat-out failures, at least for the

00:00:30.529 --> 00:00:34.610
West. Despite Sunshine promises and
predictions at the time, they led neither

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:39.200
to denuclearization nor to peace. Why
exactly should we think a third summit

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:43.489
with a third ruler of the Kim family
regime will turn out differently? True

00:00:43.489 --> 00:00:46.969
peace with the South would require
Pyongyang to recognize the right of the

00:00:46.969 --> 00:00:51.469
South Korean state to exist. True
denuclearization would force the Kim

00:00:51.469 --> 00:00:55.219
family regime to give up its quest for
unconditional unification of the whole

00:00:55.219 --> 00:01:00.079
peninsula. The real existing North Korean
state cannot accept either of these

00:01:00.079 --> 00:01:04.699
propositions. Seoul's illusions therefore
look to be on a collision course with

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:08.720
reality, and maybe Washington's, too. Stay
tuned. What do you think the outcome of

00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:10.780
What do you think the outcome of

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:14.600
the summit will be? Let us know in your
comments. Also, let us know what other

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:18.830
topics you'd like our scholars to cover
in 60 seconds, and be sure to like and

00:01:18.830 --> 00:01:23.439
subscribe for more research and videos
from AEI.

